# ── Sri Dwar — environment variables ────────────────────────────────────
# This file is a TEMPLATE only — copy it to a real .env file (which is
# git-ignored on purpose) and fill in real values there. Never put real
# secrets in this file, since it IS committed to git.
#
# NOTE: this file was recreated on 2026-09-03 after being accidentally
# deleted in an earlier commit. Built directly from scanning server.ts /
# certificateService.ts / src/ for every env var actually read by the code
# — not copied from memory — so it should be complete and accurate as of
# that scan.

# ── Supabase ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SUPABASE_URL / SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY: server-side only, full-access —
# never prefix these with VITE_ or they'd ship to every visitor's browser.
SUPABASE_URL=""
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=""
SUPABASE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=""
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL: same value as SUPABASE_URL above, just under the
# VITE_ prefix Vite requires to expose anything to the browser bundle.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=""
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY: the ANON/PUBLIC key from Supabase Dashboard ->
# Settings -> API — NOT the service role key above. The anon key is
# specifically designed to be safe for the browser; the service role key
# never is.
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=""

# ── Razorpay Payment Gateway ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Get RAZORPAY_KEY_ID / RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET from Razorpay Dashboard ->
# Account & Settings -> API keys. Use rzp_test_... values for local/dev
# testing, rzp_live_... only once ready to accept real payments.
RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=""
RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=""
# Same value as RAZORPAY_KEY_ID above, under the VITE_ prefix so the
# Checkout button (running in the browser) can read it too. Never create a
# VITE_RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET — the secret stays server-side only, always.
VITE_RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=""
# RAZORPAY_LINK_SECRET: NOT issued by Razorpay — make this up yourself
# (any long random string, e.g. `node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"`).
# Authenticates the one server endpoint (/api/razorpay/create-payment-link)
# that your Google Apps Script payment-reminder email calls — set the
# SAME value here and as a Script Property of the same name in Apps
# Script's Project Settings.
RAZORPAY_LINK_SECRET=""

# ── Cloudflare Turnstile (bot protection on public forms) ──────────────
# Get both from Cloudflare Dashboard -> Turnstile -> your site's widget.
# TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY is server-only. Leaving both blank disables the
# feature entirely (every form behaves exactly as if Turnstile didn't
# exist — see src/utils/turnstile.ts's fail-open design) rather than
# breaking anything, so it's safe to leave unset until you're ready.
TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=""
VITE_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=""

# ── Certificate / email admin endpoints ─────────────────────────────
# Both required together for the x-admin-secret-protected certificate
# image routes Google Apps Script calls into (see config.gs's
# SRIDWAR_ADMIN_API_BASE Script Property, which points AT this server —
# that property lives in Apps Script, not here).
CERTIFICATE_ADMIN_SECRET=""
EMAIL_WEBHOOK_SECRET=""
GAS_EMAIL_WEBHOOK_URL=""
# ✅ ADDED (2026-09-06 — found missing during a full audit of this file):
# both needed for the Live Certificate feature specifically. Same webhook
# deployment/URL as GAS_EMAIL_WEBHOOK_URL above (see webhook.gs's single
# doPost dispatcher, routed by a "route" field in the request body) — these
# are just their own separate secrets, checked inside that same dispatcher.
# GAS_DRIVE_UPLOAD_SECRET: protects the devotee-photo-to-Drive upload route
#   (certificatePhotoDrive.gs). Same value must also be set as a Script
#   Property in Apps Script.
# GAS_CERTIFICATE_SYNC_SECRET: protects the Certificate Generation Sheet
#   sync + acknowledgement email + "Share via Email" routes
#   (certificateGenerationSync.gs). Same value must also be set as a
#   Script Property in Apps Script.
GAS_DRIVE_UPLOAD_SECRET=""
GAS_CERTIFICATE_SYNC_SECRET=""
# ✅ ADDED (2026-09-06 — also found missing): who gets Live Certificate
# access. Comma-separated email lists, no spaces needed around commas.
# ADMIN_EMAILS: Sri Dwar staff — full access (view/edit/delete any
#   certificate, manage the shared City/Deity/Temple/Service dropdowns).
# TRIAL_VENDOR_EMAILS: lets a specific vendor account use the feature
#   (fill/photo/print only, same as a real paying vendor) without an
#   active paid subscription_tier — for testing the vendor experience
#   before it's live for real customers.
ADMIN_EMAILS=""
TRIAL_VENDOR_EMAILS=""

# ── AI Assistant ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
GEMINI_API_KEY=""

# ── Google Forms sync — form IDs ────────────────────────────────────
